From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 08:19:24 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 05/11] arm64: dts: qcom: kaanapali: Add the ICE OPP table

The UFS host scales its clocks with the UFS OPP table (75, 100 and
403 MHz). With ICE clock scaling the inline crypto engine follows it,
but only with an OPP table of its own; without one its core clock
stays at the rate it was left at.

Add the ICE OPP table with the UFS table's three rates and their CX
levels. The ICE core clock source has the same plan (75, 100, 201.5
and 403 MHz from GPLL0 / GPLL4); 201.5 MHz is left out, as the UFS
table does not use it and its level is not described here.

Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali.dtsi | 21 +++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 21 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali.dtsi
index 28cfa0bdbf10..39667f09a19a 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali.dtsi
@@ -2894,6 +2894,27 @@
 			clock-names = "core",
 				      "iface";
 			power-domains = <&gcc GCC_UFS_PHY_GDSC>;
+
+			operating-points-v2 = <&ice_opp_table>;
+
+			ice_opp_table: opp-table {
+				compatible = "operating-points-v2";
+
+				opp-75000000 {
+					opp-hz = /bits/ 64 <75000000>;
+					required-opps = <&rpmhpd_opp_low_svs_d1>;
+				};
+
+				opp-100000000 {
+					opp-hz = /bits/ 64 <100000000>;
+					required-opps = <&rpmhpd_opp_low_svs>;
+				};
+
+				opp-403000000 {
+					opp-hz = /bits/ 64 <403000000>;
+					required-opps = <&rpmhpd_opp_nom>;
+				};
+			};
 		};
 
 		cryptobam: dma-controller@1dc4000 {
